Synthetic order, fill, position and account event fixtures (decision 0009). Nothing in this
directory was received from Paradex or belongs to an account.

- Every frame here is hand-built from Paradex's published SBE schema (see README.md). Each
  OrderEvent, FillEvent, PositionEvent and AccountEvent carries a 32-byte `account` field; in
  every frame it is the made-up bytes a0, a1, ... bf, which are not a Starknet account address
  of the owner or of anyone else.
- The REST responses (`rest-*.json`) are hand-built in the shapes docs.paradex.trade
  documents; each order's and position's `account` is the same made-up bytes a0 ... bf, in hex.
- The JSON-RPC replies (`reply-*.json`, `error-*.json`) are hand-built in the shapes
  docs.paradex.trade documents; each order's `account` is the same made-up bytes a0 ... bf, in
  hex, and the error messages marked `synthetic` are made up.
- The client ids are either ids this library mints in the tests' namespace (computed from the
  test's namespace, account key and start time, see the test) or a random version 4 UUID; the
  order ids, fill and trade ids, request ids, sequences, timestamps, prices, sizes, fees and
  realized amounts, positions, average entries, collateral and account values are made-up
  inputs.

This marker covers fixtures/paradex/exec/ only. Recorded Paradex frames never go here.
